{"packet_id":"X002-01","doc_id":"X002","jurisdiction":"Jersey City, NJ","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Jersey City Rent Control Ordinance annual rent increase cap","requirement":"A landlord may not request or receive a rent increase greater than 4% or the change in the consumer price index, whichever is less, and may take only one such increase in any 12-month period. Increases at any time other than lease expiration or termination are void.","key_value":"4% or CPI change, whichever is less","coverage_conditions":"Rental housing space in Jersey City, except dwellings with four or fewer housing spaces, hotels or motels, commercial space, new 25+ unit redevelopment dwellings, low rent public housing, and buildings converted to dwelling use on or after October 1, 1983.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"units","role":"exempt","op":"at_most","n":4},{"type":"other","role":"exempt","text":"Newly constructed dwellings with 25 or more units in a redevelopment area approved by the City Council"},{"type":"other","role":"exempt","text":"Low rent public housing developments"},{"type":"other","role":"exempt","text":"Buildings converted from nonpermanent dwelling use on or after October 1, 1983"}],"per_tenancy":"New dwellings or housing spaces rented for the first time are exempt for the initial rental only.","coverage_quotes":["Dwellings with four or less housing spaces; provided, however, that this exemption shall be suspended for non-owner occupied dwellings with four or less housing spaces until the end of the state of emergency or six months from adoption of these amendments whichever comes first.","Newly constructed dwellings with 25 or more dwelling units located within a redevelopment area as defined in Section 5 of the Redevelopment Agencies Law, N.J.S.A. 40:55C-5(o), for which the City Council has approved a redevelopment plan, in accordance with Section 17 of the Redevelopment Agencies Law, N.J.S.A. 40:55C-17.","All buildings or structures, hotels, motels or guesthouses which are converted from any previous use as a nonpermanent dwelling to use as a dwelling on or after October 1, 1983."]},"exemptions":"Four-or-fewer-housing-space dwellings (exemption suspended for non-owner-occupied dwellings during the state of emergency); licensed hotels or motels; commercial and industrial space; newly built dwellings of 25 or more units in a redevelopment area; low rent public housing; buildings converted to dwelling use on or after October 1, 1983.","penalty":"Any rent increase in excess of that authorized is void, and the excess rent must be refunded or credited by the landlord forthwith.","effective_date":"2021-03-15","valid_through":null,"citation":"Jersey City Mun. Code ch. 260","quoted_span":"no landlord of any dwelling as defined in § 260-1 may request or receive a percentage increase in rent which is greater than four percent or the percentage difference between the consumer price index three months prior to the expiration or termination of the lease and three months prior to the commencement of the lease term, whichever is less.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"X002-01","doc_id":"X002","jurisdiction":"Jersey City, NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Jersey City just cause for eviction standard","requirement":"Just cause for eviction means the landlord recovered possession of a housing space or dwelling for one of the reasons outlined in State law, N.J.S.A. 2A:18-53 as amended or N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1 et seq.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental housing space in Jersey City, except dwellings with four or fewer housing spaces, hotels or motels, commercial space, new 25+ unit redevelopment dwellings, low rent public housing, and buildings converted to dwelling use on or after October 1, 1983.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"units","role":"exempt","op":"at_most","n":4},{"type":"other","role":"exempt","text":"Newly constructed dwellings with 25 or more units in a redevelopment area approved by the City Council"},{"type":"other","role":"exempt","text":"Low rent public housing developments"},{"type":"other","role":"exempt","text":"Buildings converted from nonpermanent dwelling use on or after October 1, 1983"}],"per_tenancy":"New dwellings or housing spaces rented for the first time are exempt for the initial rental only.","coverage_quotes":["Dwellings with four or less housing spaces; provided, however, that this exemption shall be suspended for non-owner occupied dwellings with four or less housing spaces until the end of the state of emergency or six months from adoption of these amendments whichever comes first.","Newly constructed dwellings with 25 or more dwelling units located within a redevelopment area as defined in Section 5 of the Redevelopment Agencies Law, N.J.S.A. 40:55C-5(o), for which the City Council has approved a redevelopment plan, in accordance with Section 17 of the Redevelopment Agencies Law, N.J.S.A. 40:55C-17."]},"exemptions":"Four-or-fewer-housing-space dwellings (exemption suspended for non-owner-occupied dwellings during the state of emergency); licensed hotels or motels; commercial and industrial space; newly built dwellings of 25 or more units in a redevelopment area; low rent public housing; buildings converted to dwelling use on or after October 1, 1983.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Jersey City Mun. Code § 260-1","quoted_span":"JUST CAUSE FOR EVICTION—That the landlord recovered possession of a housing space or dwelling for one of the reasons outlined in State law (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-53 as amended or N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1 et seq.).","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.6,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
